    <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"QAPage","name":"Long Running Temporal Workflow","datePublished":"2024-11-01T02:52:14.279Z","mainEntity":{"@type":"Question","answerCount":5,"author":{"@type":"Person","name":"krish","url":"https://community.temporal.io/u/krish"},"dateModified":"2024-11-01T02:52:14.347Z","datePublished":"2024-11-01T02:52:14.279Z","name":"Long Running Temporal Workflow","text":"I have a long running temporal workflow, some instance of which can continue running indefinitely. I understand that workflows are deterministic, however is there a way to update my workflow logic without restarting it? I understand versioning is an option however for my indefinitely running workflo&hellip;","upvoteCount":0,"suggestedAnswer":[{"@type":"Answer","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"tihomir","url":"https://community.temporal.io/u/tihomir"},"dateModified":"2024-11-01T18:56:41.223Z","datePublished":"2024-11-01T18:56:41.212Z","text":"Sounds like you will have to address event history size and count limits for single execution in your case. Once an execution hits these limits it would get terminated by service.\n\nYou should be able to apply changes using versioning. Did you run into any issues with it? Temporal test env also provi&hellip;","upvoteCount":0,"url":"https://community.temporal.io/t/long-running-temporal-workflow/14943/2"},{"@type":"Answer","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"tihomir","url":"https://community.temporal.io/u/tihomir"},"dateModified":"2024-11-01T18:58:56.209Z","datePublished":"2024-11-01T18:58:56.196Z","text":"For activity question, no that wouldnt be a change you have to version.\n\nContinueasnew completes current exec and atomically creates new one with same wfid. The continued exec is a new execution and it would run your workflow code from beginning. It does not increment versions as those directives ar&hellip;","upvoteCount":0,"url":"https://community.temporal.io/t/long-running-temporal-workflow/14943/3"},{"@type":"Answer","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"krish","url":"https://community.temporal.io/u/krish"},"dateModified":"2024-11-11T04:07:55.588Z","datePublished":"2024-11-11T04:07:55.574Z","text":"Thanks <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/tihomir\">@tihomir<\/a> for your response.\n\nWhat do you mean by “address event history size and count limits for single execution”? Doesn’t continueAsNew address the event history size?\n\nIf you say continueAsNew does not increment workflow version I am not sure how I could version the workflow if I have an &hellip;","upvoteCount":0,"url":"https://community.temporal.io/t/long-running-temporal-workflow/14943/4"},{"@type":"Answer","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"tihomir","url":"https://community.temporal.io/u/tihomir"},"dateModified":"2024-11-12T13:17:00.516Z","datePublished":"2024-11-12T13:17:00.503Z","text":"What do you mean by “address event history size and count limits for single execution” ? Doesn’t continueAsNew address the event history size?\n\nyes, should check the isContinueAsNewSuggested flag see if true to decide to contiunueasnew, this flag addresses both event history count and size (is set&hellip;","upvoteCount":0,"url":"https://community.temporal.io/t/long-running-temporal-workflow/14943/5"},{"@type":"Answer","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"tihomir","url":"https://community.temporal.io/u/tihomir"},"dateModified":"2024-11-12T13:20:07.374Z","datePublished":"2024-11-12T13:20:07.359Z","text":"If you say continueAsNew does not increment workflow version I am not sure how I could version the workflow if I have an Indefinitely running workflow?\n\ni think these are mutually exclusive, as in you can apply versioned changed to your workflow (see versioning/patching api in docs for your specif&hellip;","upvoteCount":0,"url":"https://community.temporal.io/t/long-running-temporal-workflow/14943/6"}]}}</script>
